        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 145 adds support for Column wrapping for multicol, which includes the <code class=\"notranslate\">column-height</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">column-wrap</code> properties. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5176206485618688\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5176206485618688</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">BCD already includes data for <code class=\"notranslate\">column-height</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">column-wrap</code>, but the update also includes <code class=\"notranslate\">column-height</code> as a component of the <code class=\"notranslate\">columns</code> shorthand property.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a sub-data point for <code class=\"notranslate\">column-height</code> inside<code class=\"notranslate\">columns</code>.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28923",
            "title": "Chrome 145 adds `<column-height>` in CSS `columns` shorthand",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-02T15:06:22.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-27T09:21:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
