        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1795135?u=8b4759f2d0964426ac6f2aeacf061ad1ee0e24db&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://webstatus.dev/features/input-color-alpha\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webstatus.dev/features/input-color-alpha</a></p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28903",
            "title": "Map alpha and colorspace attributes to web features",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-03T15:48:30.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-24T08:02:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "nt1m",
                "url": "https://github.com/nt1m"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome is updating the device memory limits, removing older limits and adding newer ones. It would be good to document what limits are supported.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Difficult to test all memory types without access to devices of all memory type but here's proof that the 8GB cap no longer applies:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/539919768-6d815170-aa1d-4664-9889-02f54c6a5665.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..MXYTXDpN2Q4BXyHpW0DOVl5bdO2G33vFgkZesiPZ_Og\"><img width=\"773\" height=\"252\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/539919768-6d815170-aa1d-4664-9889-02f54c6a5665.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..MXYTXDpN2Q4BXyHpW0DOVl5bdO2G33vFgkZesiPZ_Og\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 252px;\"></a></p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6330376953921536\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6330376953921536</a>.<br>\nAvailable in Chrome 146 onwards (in Chrome Canary now if you wanna test it)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">MDN PR: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3848775679\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42887\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42887/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42887\">mdn/content#42887</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28900",
            "title": "Update device memory limits",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-03T18:30:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-23T19:28:04.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds data on the individual values of the <code class=\"notranslate\">color-gamut</code> media query.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">All browsers parse the media query and all its values; see <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/mediaqueries?label=master&amp;label=experimental&amp;aligned&amp;q=feature%3Acolor-gamut\" rel=\"nofollow\">the web platform tests for feature color-gamut</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">However, Firefox does not support displays with a wider gamut (or, strictly speaking, it works only in sRGB and hands off color management to the OS), so the values other than <code class=\"notranslate\">srgb</code> are always false. This does not mean the media query is unsupported (as suggested by <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2022123523\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21422\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21422/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21422\">#21422</a>). This is the correct behavior given by the spec (emphasis added):</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">the approximate range of colors that are supported by the UA <strong>and</strong> output device</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This might be slightly surprising if you have a P3 display connected. I've added notes to capture this nuance, similar to what I've done in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3833862649\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28868\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28868/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28868\">#28868</a>.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #21422.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2022123523\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21422\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21422/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/21422\">#21422</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This came up in resolving <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3325513999\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3227\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3227/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3227\">web-platform-dx/web-features#3227</a>.</p>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28892",
            "title": "Add `color-gamut` media query value subfeatures",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-30T10:23:47.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-22T18:08:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 supports the <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> pseudo-element, which allows custom styling to be applied to browser search results; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We already have BCD for <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code>, however, you can combine <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> with the <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> pseudo-class to style the currently-highlighted search term on the page. This currently doesn't have any BCD, so I am using this PR to add <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm assuming it makes sense to put Chrome 144 down for this as well, as previously, there was no context in which <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> was supported. However, you might have other opinions on this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also thought about putting <code class=\"notranslate\">\"partial_implementation\": \"true\"</code> for this, but then again, <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> is fully supported in the context it is supported in. It just isn't supported in other contexts.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28882",
            "title": "Chrome 144 :current support",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-03T12:43:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-21T18:28:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286386?u=bc4894b945491e0834d2306dade7fef748ddf698&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Added <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;input type=\"time\"&gt;</code> time-picker note for Firefox</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Test in FF 149 with pref <code class=\"notranslate\">dom.forms.datetime.timepicker</code></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42840\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42840/hovercard\">Content PR</a></li>\n<li>Associated Bugs:\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzil.la/1726108\" rel=\"nofollow\">#1726108</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzil.la/1990226\" rel=\"nofollow\">#1990226</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2011427\" rel=\"nofollow\">#2011427</a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28873",
            "title": "Firefox `datetime-local` input time picker is behind pref",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-02T14:46:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-20T14:55:14.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dletorey",
                "url": "https://github.com/dletorey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/27905767?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">…n text-decoration-style</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Observed in experiment.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Indicated Chrome 87-88 supports <code class=\"notranslate\">text-decoration-thickness</code> when <code class=\"notranslate\">text-decoration-style</code> is not <code class=\"notranslate\">solid</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tested by visually checking in Chrome 87-88.<br>\nTest case:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-text-html-basic notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"&lt;!doctype html&gt;\n&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: solid underline 10px&quot;&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: double underline 10px&quot;&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: dotted underline 10px&quot;&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: dashed underline 10px&quot;&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: wavy underline 3px&quot;&gt;test&lt;/span&gt;&lt;!-- 10px was invisible --&gt;\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-c1\">&lt;!doctype html<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span></span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">style</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">text-decoration: solid underline 10px</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>test<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">style</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">text-decoration: double underline 10px</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>test<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">style</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">text-decoration: dotted underline 10px</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>test<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">style</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">text-decoration: dashed underline 10px</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>test<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">style</span>=\"<span class=\"pl-s\">text-decoration: wavy underline 3px</span>\"<span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span>test<span class=\"pl-kos\">&lt;/</span><span class=\"pl-ent\">span</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">&gt;</span><span class=\"pl-c\">&lt;!-- 10px was invisible --&gt;</span></pre></div>\n",
